          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: il baccano",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "il baccano — \"the racket, the uproar\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "I vicini fanno un baccano tremendo. The neighbours are making a dreadful racket."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Informal; fare baccano — to make a racket."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "baccano is built on baccanale 'a wild party', a learned borrowing from Latin bacchānal, a feast of the Greek wine god (EtymDB)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
